cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UV-Vis Spectrum Studio in research, please cite the software release used in your work."
title: "UV-Vis Spectrum Studio"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hasan
    given-names: Abdulsalam S.
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abd19990044-commits/uv-vis-spectrum-studio"
url: "https://github.com/abd19990044-commits/uv-vis-spectrum-studio"
abstract: >-
  UV-Vis Spectrum Studio is an open-source analytical spectroscopy environment
  for UV-Vis spectral processing, publication-quality visualization,
  quantitative analysis, analytical-method validation, multicomponent
  spectrophotometry, peak fitting and deconvolution, Fourier/wavelet analysis,
  chemometrics, reproducible project files, and desktop workflows.
keywords:
  - UV-Vis spectroscopy
  - analytical chemistry
  - spectrophotometry
  - chemometrics
  - method validation
  - spectral analysis
  - scientific software
